lisa-design:
- The npm fetch is opencode's background Npm.install of @opencode-ai/plugin@1.19.6 into every writable config dir (config.ts loop over ConfigPaths.directories; npm.ts reify via @npmcli/arborist). There is no switch. Prepare writes an empty node_modules/ and a package-lock.json whose root ("") depends on @opencode-ai/plugin into the generated config dir: npm.ts's install returns without reifying when node_modules exists and every declared name is in the lock root's dependencies. The package itself is not installed: nothing in the adapter's config dir imports it (no plugin/tool files).
- Rejected: npm_config_offline / registry env (leaks into the model's shell: its own npm installs would break); a read-only config dir (npm.ts skips unwritable dirs, but root passes access(W_OK) and cleanup gets harder); pre-installing the package in the image (24 MB for a package nothing uses, and the config dir is per-run scratch).
- A checkout's own .opencode/ still gets the install (OPENCODE_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG would skip it but also drops the repo's opencode config and skills); none of the target repos has one so far.
- ripgrep 15.1.0 from its release (opencode's pinned VERSION and asset targets: x86_64-unknown-linux-musl, aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu — the release has only those linux builds of each arch), in its own section before playwright so TestBaseScriptRuns' stubbed run (which ends at the GIF tools' file check) exercises its pins and asset names. No trailing [ -x ] check: sudo install under set -e already fails a bad archive.
- skipPluginInstall lives in its own file (plugin.go) and Prepare only gains the call: F1 edits prepare.go's instructions() in parallel.
